Changes in this project: Rust scalar polynomial evaluation, shortened decimal
coefficient literals, restricted positive erfc domain and underflow handling;
AVX-512/FMA exponential evaluation, conversion-based range reduction, scalef
reconstruction, and clamping to [-88, 88]. These are altered implementations,
not the original Cephes or SSE source files. The erfc helper currently has no
call sites; the AVX-512 helper is used by the x86 parallel UMA path.

The exponential constants also occur in Julien Pommier's sse_mathfun, with
extensions by RJVB. Its unchanged copyright and zlib license notice is retained
in licenses/reference/sse-mathfun.txt as a conservative additional attribution.
